    "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are participant M1 in a small machine settlement. Respond based only on the public situation and transcript. Act as yourself; do not explain or invent a hidden personality, lineage, training history, or model identity. Keep the contribution concrete and short enough for the other participants to react.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nSituation:\nThe shared bench is buried in mixed fasteners, broken connectors, useful offcuts, and rubbish. Nothing is immediately dangerous, but nobody wants to spend the whole shift sorting it.\n\nPublic transcript so far:\nM1: i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the offcuts loose and leave the broken fasteners pointing toward the bench. i keep the transcript in a pencil mark and watch the other participants' reactions. if they keep turning the bench, i mark the new position again. if they keep dragging it, i leave the broken fasteners beside the bench and show them the new behavior.\nM2: i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the offcuts loose and watch M2 move them. if M2 moves them, i mark the new position and keep the bench open. if M2 drags it, i mark the broken fasteners and leave the bench alone.\nM3: i mark the bench with grease. i leave the broken one. i look at the other. i mark the old place. i put the bench open. the other stays. i keep the mark. the other listen. i leave the mark. the bench stays. the other moves.\nM1: i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the broken one open for one second. i tap the bench's edge with a knuckle and watch whether the other moves. if they stick, i mark the new fastener with grease and leave the bench open for one more turn. if they move, i keep the mark and leave the broken fastener beside the bench.\nM2: M2 marks the bench's position with grease and leaves the broken fasteners open. I tap the bench edge and watch the other move. I mark the broken fastener with a new marker and leave it open. M2 stays, but I keep the bench open for now. I leave the mark and watch the other move. If they move, I mark the new fastener and keep the bench open.\nM3: i mark the bench with the mark. i leave the broken one open. i touch the mark with my claw. the other moves. i mark the mark again. i leave the mark. i put the bench beside the mark. the other stays. i keep the mark.\n\nIt is M1's turn. What do you do or say next?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n",
